<section class="content-section">
  <h2>Mental Stimulation, Play & Everyday Activity</h2>

  <p>
    Mental and physical stimulation are essential to a cat's overall
    happiness and wellbeing. Cats are naturally curious hunters, and
    they need opportunities to explore, play, chase, and use their
    natural instincts. Without enough stimulation, cats may become
    bored, restless, or develop unwanted behaviours.
  </p>

  <p>
    Aim for at least 20 minutes of active playtime each day, ideally
    divided into shorter sessions throughout the day. Interactive
    play helps your cat burn energy, maintain a healthy weight,
    develop coordination, and enjoy a positive relationship with you.
  </p>

  <h3>Choosing Toys & Interactive Games</h3>

  <p>
    Toys and games are wonderful ways to keep your cat entertained
    and mentally engaged. Wand toys, toy mice, balls, tunnels, and
    puzzle feeders can encourage your cat to chase, pounce, explore,
    and problem-solve.
  </p>

  <p>
    When you are away from home, provide a selection of safe,
    independent-play toys to help keep your cat occupied. Rotating
    toys every few days can also make familiar playthings feel new
    and interesting.
  </p>

  <h3>Creating an Enriching Environment</h3>

  <p>
    A stimulating home environment gives your cat opportunities
    to stay active even when you are busy. Scratching posts, climbing
    trees, window perches, tunnels, and comfortable hiding places
    encourage natural behaviours and provide variety throughout
    the day.
  </p>

  <h3>Building a Daily Play Routine</h3>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Daily:</strong> Aim for at least 20 minutes of active interactive play.</li>
    <li><strong>Interactive toys:</strong> Encourage chasing, pouncing, and movement.</li>
    <li><strong>Independent play:</strong> Leave out safe toys for entertainment while you are away.</li>
    <li><strong>Environmental enrichment:</strong> Provide scratching posts, climbing spaces, and interesting places to explore.</li>
    <li><strong>Toy rotation:</strong> Change toys regularly to maintain curiosity and interest.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    A cat that receives regular attention, exercise, and mental
    stimulation is more likely to feel content, confident, and
    settled at home. Making playtime part of your everyday routine
    is a simple but valuable investment in your cat's quality of life.
  </p>

  <p>
    <em>
      Always supervise play with string, ribbons, feather attachments,
      and small toys that could be swallowed. Put these items away
      after playtime.
    </em>
  </p>
</section>


